From: PowOS <powos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: KGSL counts every surface commit per site

KWin's window task counted ~2 damaged commits per drawn Broforce frame once 0013 flipped the game's buffers (kwin
3.65 probe: 368-430 commits / 5 s for 200 drawn; kwin_wayland 14 %, its composite only ~4 %), while Xwayland's own
lines showed ~30 flips/s and ~0.2 window-buffer commits/s - the second commit per frame had no name. Every
wl_surface.commit now goes through XWL_KGSL_SURFACE_COMMIT(site): flip, post-damage, pointer-hint (a locked
pointer's cursor position hint), input-shape, surface-id, configure, cursor; with how many carried damage (KWin
redraws only for those), the frame callbacks that came back and the Present frame timers that fired instead (0013's
100 ms KGSL timeout). One "surface commits" line per 30 s on KGSL (xwayland-kgsl-commit-stats.h,
test/commit-stats-test.c).
---
diff --git a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-cursor.c b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-cursor.c
index fa77f6d..3711ccd 100644
--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-cursor.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-cursor.c
@@ -33,6 +33,7 @@
 #include "mipointer.h"
 
 #include "xwayland-cursor.h"
+#include "xwayland-kgsl-commit-stats.h"
 #include "xwayland-input.h"
 #include "xwayland-pixmap.h"
 #include "xwayland-screen.h"
@@ -164,7 +165,7 @@ xwl_cursor_attach_pixmap(struct xwl_seat *xwl_seat,
                                      xwl_cursor_buffer_release_callback,
                                      pixmap);
 
-    wl_surface_commit(xwl_cursor->surface);
+    XWL_KGSL_SURFACE_COMMIT(XWL_COMMIT_CURSOR, xwl_cursor->surface);  /* PowOS 0014 */
 }
 
 Bool
